<title>RUSSIA: UES jumps to record 34 cents on GDR news.</title>
<headline>UES jumps to record 34 cents on GDR news.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in national power company RAO Yedinaya Energeticheskaya Sistema Rossii (UES) jumped to a record $0.3400 at 0907 GMT after news that trading in a non-U.S. global depositary receipt (GDR) would start on Monday.</p>
<p>UES closed on Thursday, the previous trading day in Russia, at $0.2798, and rose in early trading to $0.3150 on rumours of the GDR issue.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
